# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored pattern like "data/"
# matches at ANY depth, which would also exclude src/data (the content the
# build reads) and break the deploy.

# Local runtime storage at the repo root
/data/

# The uploaded photographs. They stay in the repo, next to everything else in
# assets, because that is where they were put and where the next one will go —
# but they are source files, not pages. scripts/build-photos.py derives the
# web-sized crops into public/assets/photo/ and those are what the site serves,
# so the deploy never carries the 46 MB of originals.
#
# Every PNG in this directory is an original by convention; the generated
# artwork lives in assets/photo (crops), assets/brand (logo, favicons, link
# card) and assets/img/ph-*.svg (placeholders). scripts/check-vercel-upload.js
# proves no built page ever points at a file this drops.
/public/assets/img/*.png

# Not needed by the deployment
/docs/
/supabase/
/test/
/.github/
*.log
